WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.007 --> 00:00:08.331
Joe Biden's win may be a double-edged sword for teachers unions.

00:00:08.688 --> 00:00:12.220
Teachers unions worked hard to elect Biden, a long time ally.

00:00:12.562 --> 00:00:14.482
And public support for teachers is high.

00:00:14.891 --> 00:00:17.497
Many parents express a new found appreciation

00:00:17.497 --> 00:00:19.509
for just how exhausting the job can be.

00:00:19.822 --> 00:00:23.299
Yet, as school systems around the country shut their doors,

00:00:23.299 --> 00:00:28.119
or delay reopening despite mounting evidence that in-person learning can be done safely,

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:30.625
parents' patience is wearing thin.

00:00:30.714 --> 00:00:35.254
Until now, President Trump's reckless calls for schools to open immediately

00:00:35.254 --> 00:00:38.159
have allowed unions to portray their resistance to reopening 

00:00:38.159 --> 00:00:40.434
as the "responsible" position.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.918
With Trump gone, that changes.

00:00:42.918 --> 00:00:46.666
If Biden is wearing a mask and pushing for more school funds,

00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:50.969
It'll be tough for unions to insist that reopening is just a Trumpian rush

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:52.407
back to business as usual.

00:00:52.407 --> 00:00:55.726
Under President Biden, unions will face a clear choice: 

00:00:55.726 --> 00:00:58.488
Help lead on responsibly reopening schools,  

00:00:58.488 --> 00:01:02.435
or risk stoking concerns that they're more focused on member convenience

00:01:02.435 --> 00:01:04.100
than student wellbeing. 

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.599
Their choice will be telling.

00:01:07.328 --> 00:01:10.554
Do you think teachers and schools have risen to the challenge of COVID?

00:01:10.584 --> 00:01:12.000
Let us know in our poll.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.437
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:16.437 --> 00:01:20.939
And be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

